{"id":"mahabharata-3-017","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":17,"title":"सप्तदशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 17 · The Vrishnis defend the city","summary":{"en":"Shalva besieges Dvaraka with a huge army. The Vrishni heroes Samba, Charudeshna and Pradyumna ride out against him, and Pradyumna rallies the Yadavas and engages Shalva's forces.","kn":"ಶಾಲ್ವನು ಮಹಾಸೈನ್ಯದೊಂದಿಗೆ ದ್ವಾರಕೆಯನ್ನು ಮುತ್ತುತ್ತಾನೆ. ವೃಷ್ಣಿವೀರರಾದ ಸಾಂಬ, ಚಾರುದೇಷ್ಣ, ಪ್ರದ್ಯುಮ್ನರು ಅವನ ವಿರುದ್ಧ ಹೊರಡುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಪ್ರದ್ಯುಮ್ನನು ಯಾದವರನ್ನು ಹುರಿದುಂಬಿಸಿ ಶಾಲ್ವನ ಸೈನ್ಯದೊಂದಿಗೆ ಹೋರಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"शाल्व विशाल सेना से द्वारका को घेरता है। वृष्णि वीर साम्ब, चारुदेष्ण और प्रद्युम्न उसके विरुद्ध निकलते हैं, और प्रद्युम्न यादवों का उत्साह बढ़ाकर शाल्व की सेना से भिड़ते हैं।","te":"శాల్వుడు మహాసైన్యంతో ద్వారకను ముట్టడిస్తాడు. వృష్ణివీరులు సాంబుడు, చారుదేష్ణుడు, ప్రద్యుమ్నుడు అతనిపై దండెత్తుతారు; ప్రద్యుమ్నుడు యాదవులను ఉత్సాహపరచి శాల్వుని సేనలతో తలపడతాడు.","ta":"ஶால்வன் பெரும் படையுடன் த்வாரகையை முற்றுகையிடுகிறான். வ்ருஷ்ணி வீரர்களான ஸாம்பன், சாருதேஷ்ணன், ப்ரத்யும்னன் அவனை எதிர்த்துப் புறப்பட, ப்ரத்யும்னன் யாதவர்களுக்கு ஊக்கமளித்து ஶால்வனின் படையுடன் போரிடுகிறான்.","ml":"ശാല്വൻ വലിയ സൈന്യവുമായി ദ്വാരകയെ ഉപരോധിക്കുന്നു. വൃഷ്ണിവീരന്മാരായ സാംബനും ചാരുദേഷ്ണനും പ്രദ്യുമ്നനും അദ്ദേഹത്തെ നേരിടാൻ പുറപ്പെടുന്നു; പ്രദ്യുമ്നൻ യാദവരെ അണിനിരത്തി ശാല്വന്റെ സൈന്യവുമായി ഏറ്റുമുട്ടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.17; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"कैरातपर्व","titleEn":"Kairata Parva (The mountain hunter)","verses":[{"text":"वासुदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तां तूपयात्वा राजेन्द्र शाल्वः सौभपतिस्तदा ।\nप्रभूतनरनागेन बलेनोपविवेश ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Approaching it, king, Shalva, lord of Saubha, then encamped with a large force of many men and elephants."}},{"n":2,"text":"समे निविष्टा सा सेना प्रभूतसलिलाशये ।\nचतुरङ्गबलोपेता शाल्वराजाभिपालिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"That army, encamped on level ground near a large body of water, with its four divisions, was protected by King Shalva."}},{"n":3,"text":"वर्जयित्वा श्मशानानि देवतायतनानि च ।\nवल्मीकांश्चैव चैत्यांश्च तन्निविष्टमभूद्बलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Avoiding cremation grounds, temples, anthills and sacred trees, the force made its camp."}},{"n":4,"text":"अनीकानां विभागेन पन्थानः षट्कृताभवन् ।\nप्रवणा नव चैवासञ्शाल्वस्य शिबिरे नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"By the division of the troops six roads were made, and nine descents, in Shalva's camp, king."}},{"n":5,"text":"सर्वायुधसमोपेतं सर्वशस्त्रविशारदम् ।\nरथनागाश्वकलिलं पदातिध्वजसंकुलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was equipped with every weapon, its men skilled in all arms, crowded with chariots, elephants and horses, thick with foot-soldiers and banners."}},{"n":6,"text":"तुष्टपुष्टजनोपेतं वीरलक्षणलक्षितम् ।\nविचित्रध्वजसंनाहं विचित्ररथकार्मुकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was full of contented, well-fed men marked with the signs of heroes, with varied banners and armor, and varied chariots and bows."}},{"n":7,"text":"संनिवेश्य च कौरव्य द्वारकायां नरर्षभ ।\nअभिसारयामास तदा वेगेन पतगेन्द्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having encamped, descendant of Kuru, bull among men, he then advanced swiftly on Dvaraka like the king of birds."}},{"n":8,"text":"तदापतन्तं संदृश्य बलं शाल्वपतेस्तदा ।\nनिर्याय योधयामासुः कुमारा वृष्णिनन्दनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the force of the king of Shalva coming, the young Vrishni princes came out and fought."}},{"n":9,"text":"असहन्तोऽभियानं तच्छाल्वराजस्य कौरव ।\nचारुदेष्णश्च साम्बश्च प्रद्युम्नश्च महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Unable to bear that advance of King Shalva, Charudeshna, Samba and the great chariot-warrior Pradyumna,"}},{"n":10,"text":"ते रथैर्दंशिताः सर्वे विचित्राभरणध्वजाः ।\nसंसक्ताः शाल्वराजस्य बहुभिर्योधपुंगवैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"all armored in chariots, with varied ornaments and banners, closed with many chief warriors of Shalva."}},{"n":11,"text":"गृहीत्वा तु धनुः साम्बः शाल्वस्य सचिवं रणे ।\nयोधयामास संहृष्टः क्षेमवृद्धिं चमूपतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking up his bow, Samba, delighted, fought Shalva's counselor and army chief, Kshemavriddhi, in the battle."}},{"n":12,"text":"तस्य बाणमयं वर्षं जाम्बवत्याः सुतो महत् ।\nमुमोच भरतश्रेष्ठ यथा वर्षं सहस्रदृक् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Jambavati's son loosed a great rain of arrows on him, best of the Bharatas, like the thousand-eyed Indra sending rain."}},{"n":13,"text":"तद्बाणवर्षं तुमुलं विषेहे स चमूपतिः ।\nक्षेमवृद्धिर्महाराज हिमवानिव निश्चलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That army commander Kshemavriddhi withstood the tumultuous shower of arrows, great king, like unmoving Himalaya."}},{"n":14,"text":"ततः साम्बाय राजेन्द्र क्षेमवृद्धिरपि स्म ह ।\nमुमोच मायाविहितं शरजालं महत्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Kshemavriddhi too loosed on Samba, king, a vast net of arrows made by illusion."}},{"n":15,"text":"ततो मायामयं जालं माययैव विदार्य सः ।\nसाम्बः शरसहस्रेण रथमस्याभ्यवर्षत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Samba, breaking that illusory net with illusion itself, showered a thousand arrows on his chariot."}},{"n":16,"text":"ततः स विद्धः साम्बेन क्षेमवृद्धिश्चमूपतिः ।\nअपायाज्जवनैरश्वैः साम्बबाणप्रपीडितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pierced by Samba, the army chief Kshemavriddhi fled on his swift horses, tormented by Samba's arrows."}},{"n":17,"text":"तस्मिन्विप्रद्रुते क्रूरे शाल्वस्याथ चमूपतौ ।\nवेगवान्नाम दैतेयः सुतं मेऽभ्यद्रवद्बली ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Shalva's cruel army chief had fled, a strong Daitya named Vegavat rushed at my son."}},{"n":18,"text":"अभिपन्नस्तु राजेन्द्र साम्बो वृष्णिकुलोद्वहः ।\nवेगं वेगवतो राजंस्तस्थौ वीरो विधारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, Samba, upholder of the Vrishni line, was attacked, and the hero stood and held off Vegavat's rush."}},{"n":19,"text":"स वेगवति कौन्तेय साम्बो वेगवतीं गदाम् ।\nचिक्षेप तरसा वीरो व्याविध्य सत्यविक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son of Kunti, Samba the hero, true in valor, whirled a swift mace and hurled it quickly at Vegavat."}},{"n":20,"text":"तया त्वभिहतो राजन्वेगवानपतद्भुवि ।\nवातरुग्ण इव क्षुण्णो जीर्णमूलो वनस्पतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by it, king, Vegavat fell to the ground like a tree with rotten roots crushed by a storm."}},{"n":21,"text":"तस्मिन्निपतिते वीरे गदानुन्ने महासुरे ।\nप्रविश्य महतीं सेनां योधयामास मे सुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that great asura had fallen, struck by the mace, my son entered the great army and fought."}},{"n":22,"text":"चारुदेष्णेन संसक्तो विविन्ध्यो नाम दानवः ।\nमहारथः समाज्ञातो महाराज महाधनुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A Danava named Vivindhya, a renowned great chariot-warrior and great archer, closed with Charudeshna, great king."}},{"n":23,"text":"ततः सुतुमुलं युद्धं चारुदेष्णविविन्ध्ययोः ।\nवृत्रवासवयो राजन्यथा पूर्वं तथाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a most tumultuous fight arose between Charudeshna and Vivindhya, king, like that of Vritra and Vasava in the past."}},{"n":24,"text":"अन्योन्यस्याभिसंक्रुद्धावन्योन्यं जघ्नतुः शरैः ।\nविनदन्तौ महाराज सिंहाविव महाबलौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Enraged at each other, they struck each other with arrows, roaring, great king, like two mighty lions."}},{"n":25,"text":"रौक्मिणेयस्ततो बाणमग्न्यर्कोपमवर्चसम् ।\nअभिमन्त्र्य महास्त्रेण संदधे शत्रुनाशनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Rukmini's son charged an arrow, equal in blaze to fire and sun, with a great mantra, to destroy the enemy."}},{"n":26,"text":"स विविन्ध्याय सक्रोधः समाहूय महारथः ।\nचिक्षेप मे सुतो राजन्स गतासुरथापतत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Furious, the great chariot-warrior, my son, called Vivindhya out and hurled it, king, and he fell lifeless from his chariot."}},{"n":27,"text":"विविन्ध्यं निहतं दृष्ट्वा तां च विक्षोभितां चमूम् ।\nकामगेन स सौभेन शाल्वः पुनरुपागमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Vivindhya killed and the army thrown into disorder, Shalva came back on Saubha, which goes where it wills."}},{"n":28,"text":"ततो व्याकुलितं सर्वं द्वारकावासि तद्बलम् ।\nदृष्ट्वा शाल्वं महाबाहो सौभस्थं पृथिवीगतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all the Dvaraka forces were thrown into confusion, mighty-armed one, seeing Shalva on Saubha, though he had come down to earth."}},{"n":29,"text":"ततो निर्याय कौन्तेय व्यवस्थाप्य च तद्बलम् ।\nआनर्तानां महाराज प्रद्युम्नो वाक्यमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Pradyumna came out, son of Kunti, and arranged that force, great king, and spoke to the Anartas."}},{"n":30,"text":"सर्वे भवन्तस्तिष्ठन्तु सर्वे पश्यन्तु मां युधि ।\nनिवारयन्तं संग्रामे बलात्सौभं सराजकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All of you stay here, all of you watch me in battle as I hold back Saubha and its king by force."}},{"n":31,"text":"अहं सौभपतेः सेनामायसैर्भुजगैरिव ।\nधनुर्भुजविनिर्मुक्तैर्नाशयाम्यद्य यादवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yadavas, today I will destroy the army of the lord of Saubha with arrows of iron like serpents, loosed from the strength of my bow arm."}},{"n":32,"text":"आश्वसध्वं न भीः कार्या सौभराडद्य नश्यति ।\nमयाभिपन्नो दुष्टात्मा ससौभो विनशिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Take heart, do not be afraid; the king of Saubha is perishing today. Attacked by me, that evil one will be destroyed along with Saubha."}},{"n":33,"text":"एवं ब्रुवति संहृष्टे प्रद्युम्ने पाण्डुनन्दन ।\nविष्ठितं तद्बलं वीर युयुधे च यथासुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While Pradyumna spoke thus in delight, son of Pandu, that force held its ground, hero, and fought with ease."}}]}]}